# Git already stores every text file with LF. Without this, the working tree
# is left to each contributor's core.autocrlf: on Windows that checks files
# out as CRLF, while the JS toolchain here (biome, openapi-ts) writes them
# back as LF -- so files show as modified with no content change at all.
# That churn is not cosmetic in practice: it buries real diffs, and twice in
# one session it was mistaken for lost work.
#
# eol=lf, not just text=auto: this project's own tools emit LF regardless of
# platform, and nothing tracked here needs CRLF (no .bat/.cmd/.ps1).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Declared binary so git never tries to translate them, and never offers a
# line-diff for bytes that have no lines.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
